{"tool_name":"code","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"code","home":"https://web.iitm.ac.in/bioinfo2/codeop/landing_page.html","summary":"Tool to deoptimize the RNA or DNA sequences based on codon usage. Codon-pair deoptimization involves increasing the frequency of underrepresented codon pairs without changing codon usage or amino acid sequences.","addition_date":"2023-11-29T13:44:59.541705Z","last_update_date":"2023-11-29T13:44:59.544152Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:code","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"gromiha@iitm.ac.in","name":"M Michael Gromiha","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1776-4096","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"lmartinez@txbiomed.org","name":"Luis Martinez-Sobrido","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"nogales.aitor@inia.csic.es","name":"Aitor Nogales","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Codon usage bias calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2962"},{"term":"Codon usage table generation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0284"},{"term":"Formatting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0335"},{"term":"Genetic code prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0489"}]}],"name":"CoDe","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOADV/VBAC102","metadata":{"abstract":"We have developed a web-based tool, CoDe (Codon Deoptimization) that deoptimizes genetic sequences based on different codon usage bias, ultimately reducing expression of the corresponding protein. The tool could also deoptimize the sequence for a specific region and/or selected amino acid(s). Moreover, CoDe can highlight sites targeted by restriction enzymes in the wild-type and codon-deoptimized sequences. Importantly, our web-based tool has a user-friendly interface with flexible options to download results.","authors":[{"name"